      ":question/id": "9523d8a1-3d40-572c-a11e-74892867a41f",
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/easy",
      ":question/problem": "Consider a $8\\times 6$ matrix $A.$ If $\\text{rank}(A)=5$ then $\\text{nullity}(A)=$",
      ":question/worked-solution": "According to the rank-nullity theorem, if $A$ is a matrix with $n$ columns, then \n\n$$\n\\text{rank}(A)+\\text{nullity}(A)=n.\n$$\n\nFor the given matrix, we have $n=6.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{rank}(A)+\\text{nullity}(A) & =n \\\\ 5+\\text{nullity}(A) & =6 \\\\ \\text{nullity}(A) & =6-5 \\\\  & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
